cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MerMED-FM, please cite the paper below."
title: "MerMED-FM: Multimodal, Multi-Disease Medical Imaging Foundation Model"
abstract: >-
  MerMED-FM is a self-supervised, multi-specialty medical imaging foundation
  model. A ViT-B/16 backbone is pretrained with a DINO-style teacher-student
  objective extended with a feature/label memory bank, random prototype
  partitioning, and a KoLeo regularizer, across seven imaging modalities: color
  fundus photography, optical coherence tomography, chest X-ray, CT,
  histopathology, ultrasound, and dermatology. This repository contains the
  pretraining, finetuning, evaluation, and explainability code.
type: software
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/yangzhou12/MerMED"
url: "https://github.com/yangzhou12/MerMED"
keywords:
  - foundation model
  - medical imaging
  - self-supervised learning
  - vision transformer
  - multimodal
